# Implementation Plan: In-Store Product Reservation & Item Hold (O2O) - Phase 2

Enable customers to hold/reserve products for physical in-store pickup, preventing items from being sold out while traveling to the store. Includes 6-digit pickup codes, auto-expiration, and a shopkeeper verification terminal.

---

## User Flow & Design

```
[ Customer ]
     │
     ├── 1. POST /reservations (Reserve product, default 4-hour hold)
     │       └── Generates Reservation Number (e.g. HLD-729401) & 6-digit Pickup Code (e.g. 842910)
     │       └── Locks inventory: increases `inventory.reserved_quantity`
     │
     ├── 2. GET /reservations (View active reservations with timer, shop address & maps link)
     │
     └── 3. Visits physical shop & shows 6-digit Pickup Code to shopkeeper
                                   │
                                   ▼
                            [ Shopkeeper ]
                                   │
     ┌─────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────┐
     ▼                                                           ▼
POST /shops/me/reservations/verify                       POST /shops/me/reservations/{id}/cancel
(Enters 6-digit code at billing counter)                 (If customer doesn't show up or out of stock)
- Verifies pickup code                                   - Releases inventory hold
- Marks reservation `completed`                          - Sets status to `cancelled`/`expired`
- Deducts product inventory stock
```

