### 4. Service & Controller Layer
#### [NEW] [services/reservation.go](file:///c:/Go/shopMe/internal/handler/services/reservation.go)
- Enforce business logic:
  - Check product availability (`quantity - reserved_quantity >= requested_qty`).
  - Max active reservations per customer limit (e.g., max 3 active holds to prevent hoarding).
  - Secure random 6-digit `pickup_code` generator.
  - Expiry calculation based on `hold_hours`.

#### [NEW] [controller/reservation.go](file:///c:/Go/shopMe/internal/handler/controller/reservation.go)
- Customer Endpoints:
  - `POST /reservations` — Create hold request.
  - `GET /reservations` — List my reservations.
  - `GET /reservations/{id}` — View reservation details.
  - `POST /reservations/{id}/cancel` — Cancel hold request.
- Shopkeeper Endpoints:
  - `GET /shops/me/reservations` — List reservations for my shop.
  - `POST /shops/me/reservations/verify` — Verify customer's 6-digit code at counter.
  - `POST /shops/me/reservations/{id}/cancel` — Reject/cancel hold from shop side.

